<WikiLayout title="About WARDOGS Wiki" description="About the independent WARDOGS Wiki knowledge database, its scope and version-bound approach." canonicalPath="/about/" pageType="AboutPage">
  <h1>About WARDOGS Wiki</h1><p>WARDOGS Wiki is an independent game knowledge database built to connect guides, entities and battlefield systems without presenting unsupported values as fact. It is designed for players who need both a quick answer and a clear path to the surrounding context.</p>
  <h2>Mission</h2><p>The project turns scattered game information into a navigable reference. Hub pages explain systems, entity records organize individual weapons, vehicles and maps, and relationship links show how those records connect to loadouts, progression, economy and objective play.</p>
  <h2>Scope</h2><p>Current coverage includes maps, weapons, vehicles, economy, loadouts, progression, factions, construction and community servers. Version-sensitive entries identify the Season 1 / Patch 0.11 snapshot. Information that cannot be supported is labeled <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong> rather than converted into a precise claim.</p>
  <h2>How to use the Wiki</h2><p>New players can begin with <a href="/how-to-play/">How To Play WARDOGS</a>. Readers looking for a specific item can browse the <a href="/database/">Game Database</a>, while the <a href="/tools/">Tools</a> help narrow down a loadout or comparison before opening the full records.</p>
  <h2>Independence</h2><p>This is a community-built reference and is not presented as an official Team17 publication. Official sources are prioritized for factual claims, and community observations are labeled according to the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is this an official Wiki?</h3><p>No. It is an independent reference that links to official sources where available.</p><h3>Why are some values missing?</h3><p>Omitting an unsupported value is more useful than publishing false precision. Missing or uncertain values remain <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>.</p>
</WikiLayout>
